Task 2: Change Requests and Traceability Matrix (RTM)
2.1 Version-controlled change log
Assume the approved baseline is version 1.0, and the updated version is 1.1.
CR ID	Requirement ID	Old requirement	New requirement	Reason	Status
CR-01	SAFE-01	The robot shall enter Safe Mode when a critical battery or thermal condition is detected.	The robot shall enter Safe Mode within 3 seconds when chamber or battery temperature exceeds the critical threshold or battery capacity falls below the emergency level.	Adds measurable timing and explicit triggering conditions.	Modified
CR-02	NFR-02	The system shall support communication with multiple robots simultaneously.	The system shall support at least 20 simultaneously connected robots.	Defines a minimum capacity that can be tested.	Modified
CR-03	FR-03	Only authenticated operators shall be permitted to issue robot commands.	The system shall require authenticated and role-authorised operators before accepting any robot command.	Requires both identity verification and permission verification.	Modified
Why the new wording is better
- CR-01: A test engineer can measure the time between critical-condition detection and Safe Mode entry. The limit is 3 seconds.
- CR-02: A load test can connect 20 robots simultaneously and verify that all can maintain supported communication.
- CR-03: Tests can cover unauthenticated users, authenticated users with insufficient permissions, and authenticated users with the correct role.
